verses.text:
Make a chain,
for the land is full of bloody judgment,
and the city is full of violence.

The head of its shoots he plucked,
and he brought it to the land of Canaan;
in a city of traders he put it.

With interest, he does not give,
and usury he does not take;
from perversity, he turns back his hand;
a judgment of truth he does between a man and a man;

But he, all of these he did not do—
for he even eats on the mountains,
and the wife of his neighbor he defiles;

the poor and needy he oppresses;
robberies he robs;
a pledge he does not return;
and to the idols he lifts his eyes;
an abomination he does;

On the mountains he does not eat,
and his eyes he does not lift to the idols of the house of Israel;
the wife of his neighbor he does not defile;

and a man he does not oppress;
a pledge he does not take in pledge,
and robbery he does not rob;
his bread to the hungry, he gives,
and the naked he covers with clothing;

from perversity, he turns back his hand;
interest and usury he does not take;
my judgments he does;
in my statutes, he walks—
he, he will not die in the iniquity of his father.
Living, he will live!

And she raised up one from her cubs; he became a young lion,
and he learned to tear prey;
he ate men.

And he walked about in the midst of lions;
he became a young lion,
and he learned to tear prey;
he ate men.

With toil, it has wearied,
and the abundance of its rot has not gone out from it;
into a fire, its rust!

The dwellers of Sidon and Arvad were rowers for you;
your wise men, O Tyre, were in you;
they were your rope-men.

Persia and Lud and Put were in your army, your men of war.
They hung shield and helmet in you;
they, they gave your splendor.

The sons of Arvad and your army were on your walls all around, and Gammadim were in your towers.
They hung their shields on your walls all around;
they, they perfected your beauty.

And all of the graspers of an oar will come down from their ships;
the sailors, all of the rope-men of the sea,
will stand on the land.

And they will make heard over you with their voice,
and they will cry out bitterly, and they will bring up dust on their heads;
they will roll in the ashes.

All of the dwellers of the coastlands are desolate over you,
and their kings have shuddered a shudder;
their faces have quaked.
